For each room, only guest numbers dividing its room number affect it. Modulo 3, a guest \(n\):
- \(n\equiv0\): no net effect;
- \(n\equiv1\): forces the light to red after the cat;
- \(n\equiv2\): swaps red and blue.

Counting rooms by their divisors with this rule gives 48 blue lights.

48

Between guests, no green light remains. For guest \(n\):
- \(n\equiv0\pmod3\): no net change;
- \(n\equiv1\pmod3\): affected lights end red;
- \(n\equiv2\pmod3\): affected lights flip red/blue.

For a room \(k=3^a m\) with \(m\not\equiv0\pmod3\), only divisors of \(m\) matter. Rooms with \(m\equiv1\pmod3\) end red. Rooms with \(m\equiv2\pmod3\) end blue except for the special case \(m=77\), whose effective divisor sequence \(1,7,11,77\) gives two flips after the last reset. There are \(49\) rooms with 3-free part congruent to \(2\pmod3\); excluding room \(77\) leaves \(48\).

